export anchor NightMetroStyle:
    number: 316
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Night metro
    idea: The monitor drawn as a night transit map, where each service is a coloured line running across the last 24 hours, deploys and alerts are stations on it, and trouble shows as dashed track and an amber disruption sign.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #0b1016, the page
        platform: #131a23, panels and the style sheet
        platformRaised: #1b2430, line pills and list rows
        mapWell: #0e141c, the slightly lighter well behind the map
        ink: #f1f5f9, text, the current app pill and the primary button
        muted: #a7b3c4, meta, axis times and the legend
        rail: #2c3746, borders, dashed rules and the hour grid on the map
        lineApi: #4fb3ff, the api line, the header roundel and the request chart
        lineWeb: #ff8a3d, the web line and the p95 line
        lineSync: #3ddc9c, the sync-worker line
        lineNotif: #c792ff, the notifications line and the p50 line
        lineBilling: #ffd23f, the billing line
        healthy: #5ee39a, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
        degraded: #ffc94d, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier, and notice times
        recovered: #7cc4ff, Recovered with a diamond, and links
        firing: #ff7b84, Firing octagon stations and the error line
        signAmber: #ffc94d, the disruption band with dark text
    type:
        Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Segoe UI, Arial, signage style. Base 15px
        at 1.5. The incident ID is 28px at 800, the station name 20px at
        700, panel titles 17px at 700, notice times 14px at 700 with tabular
        numbers in amber, map labels 11px at 600.
    layout:
        A near black station sign header with a roundel mark, a ring with
        a bar through it reading OPS, the Brightwork Ops name and Production
        network last 24 hours, and the suite apps as outlined pills with a
        white filled pill for Ops. Below, a full width Service lines panel
        holds the map in a scrollable well. Down the left, five lettered
        bullets A, W, S, N, B with the service name and its status shape,
        word and uptime. Five thick horizontal lines run from 10 yesterday
        to now across an hour grid. Deploys are white circle stations,
        resolved alerts white squares, the firing queue alert a red
        octagon. sync-worker turns to dashed track from the firing alert to
        now, billing has a short break with a dotted white gap and a down 6
        min note. A legend explains clear track, dashed track, break,
        deploy, resolved and firing. Next comes a row of three, an amber
        Service disruption severity 2 sign with INC-0427 and its facts and
        pill buttons, a Service notices board for alerts, and a Timetable
        changes board for deploys, each item with a lettered line pill. A
        final row of three panels holds Requests per minute, Error rate and
        Latency, each with a lettered bullet, a big figure and a thick round
        capped line chart. Below 980px rows stack, below 760px the map
        scrolls sideways inside its well.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutter, 20px panel padding and gaps, 60px between map lines.
    density: Medium. One wide map, then two rows of three panels.
    corners: 14px panels, full pills for buttons, fields, list rows and app tabs, round line bullets.
    borders: 1px rail borders on panels and dashed rules between notices. Map lines are 10px thick with round caps.
    shadows: None. The map sits on a slightly lighter well.
    icons:
        Lettered line bullets A, W, S, N, B. Map stations are a white
        circle for deploys, a white square for resolved and a red octagon
        for firing. Status words pair with a filled circle, triangle,
        diamond, octagon, square or a magnifier.
    focus: A 3px white outline offset 2px with a 6px blue halo.
    tone: Transit signage such as Service lines, Service disruption, Service notices and Timetable changes, with plain facts after.
